    "git_commit": "82e31eb4e35756a68507e49090ac0728d42c6dbb -- RECOVERED, not recorded. The sweep's own recorded_at is 2026-09-28T19:07:29+00:00 (2026-09-29 03:07 local) and the commit timeline has a gap spanning it: 82e31eb is 2026-09-28 18:25 local and the next commit, 53c5b21, is 2026-09-29 08:39. Only one commit can have been HEAD then. This is a lower bound, not a proof: the working tree at that moment need not have matched it, and nothing recorded whether it did.",
    "gigaxml": "1.1.0 -- RECOVERED from src/gigaxml/__init__.py at that commit. This file's own environment.gigaxml says 0.1.0 and is KNOWN WRONG: commit e837d7c fixed exactly that reading five and a half hours after the sweep ran ('how a sweep of 1.1.0 recorded itself as 0.1.0'). The value below is the recovered one; the wrong one is left in environment.gigaxml rather than edited, because that is what was written down at the time.",
